{"title":"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 6","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Consider an isosceles triangle. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/5/5/b55ca7a0aa88ab7d58f4fc035317fdac39b17861.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$r$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> be the radius of its circumscribed circle and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/0/2/0027034d8a10372a06deaf4f4084c01956587479.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\rho$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"9\" height=\"11\" /> the radius of its inscribed circle. Prove that the distance <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/6/a/96ab646de7704969b91c76a214126b45f2b07b25.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" /> between the centers of these two circles is \n</p>\n<center><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/b/9/0b9cd6e5d83905e2b9d1e89df0d9e333ca34da6c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$d=\\sqrt{r(r-2\\rho)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"124\" height=\"32\" />.</center>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>&lt;geogebra&gt;d1f93636341cbe0bc2f98c788171d8a55d94f8c8&lt;/geogebra&gt;\nInstead of an isosceles triangle, let us consider an arbitrary triangle <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" />. Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/2/a/e2a559986ed5a0ffc5654bd367c29dfc92913c36.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$ABC$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"44\" height=\"14\" /> have circumcenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/1/d/51da37d984564162c87710ca27bea422f657fb73.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$O$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> and incenter <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/c/bfcb6f9286d36a1d244aa1be5a7fb0e274d53ee5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"25\" height=\"14\" /> to meet the circumcircle again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/5/9/859ccf4cd60c7bc6b8fa1afc9a42dc811a826d6f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$L$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"14\" height=\"14\" />. Then extend <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/1/6/8169f7aa8a60ef728e56101134b238176c5ed804.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$LO$\" width=\"26\" height=\"12\" /> so it meets the circumcircle again at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/d/1/5d1e4485dc90c450e8c76826516c1b2ccb8fce16.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$M$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"21\" height=\"14\" />.\nConsider the point where the incircle meets <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/7/e/57ee5125358c0606c9b588580ddfa66f83e607b7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"30\" height=\"14\" />, and let this be point <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/f/f/9ffb448918db29f2a72f8f87f421b3b3cad18f95.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$D$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"17\" height=\"14\" />. We have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/8/5/9855ea1ea0039effc008ce6692b71991cc2b4877.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle ADI = \\angle MBL = 90^{\\circ}, \\angle IAD = \\angle LMB$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"328\" height=\"16\" />; thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/c/6/6c6d5acabf0e4d4618dbd3ba999cdb2f4625fbd1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\triangle ADI \\sim \\triangle MBL$\" width=\"141\" height=\"13\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/b/1/2b19f2412ca8888959802bd3bfa3d7f56bf31346.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac {ID}{BL} = \\frac {AI} {ML} \\iff ID \\cdot ML = 2r\\rho = AI \\cdot BL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"356\" height=\"39\" />.\nNow, drawing line <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/b/35bb3f3bcadf5dc5c045b80fc24d014c0b969cd4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/6/4b65336057973299e99170042ab47245d6baafcd.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\angle BIL = \\frac {1}{2}\\angle A + \\frac {1}{2}\\angle ABC, \\angle IBL = \\frac {1}{2}\\angle ABC + \\angle CBL = \\frac {1}{2}\\angle ABC + \\frac {1}{2}\\angle A$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"584\" height=\"37\" />. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/0/5/5055d07682a2f2d8742c31e5f4bb9789c012c72e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$BIL$\" width=\"36\" height=\"12\" /> is isosceles, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/9/0/5904aee079ec1010cd912ae2accb97206d6a1e2a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$IL = BL$\" width=\"72\" height=\"12\" />.\nSubstituting this back in, we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/a/b/dab5cb1a33a5a7a2c515a1c8ce37cdcd32e6ab37.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r\\rho = AI\\cdot IL$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"111\" height=\"18\" />. Extending <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/9/a/89a2556c5400ea7972b91e9f9154b1604f5995af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$OI$\" width=\"24\" height=\"12\" /> to meet the circumcircle at <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/9/d/49d559f1ae366d6c7ddffa20b504ac135a430839.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$P,Q$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"34\" height=\"16\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/5/5/755b7615123d719871c25d7a1931804d76d4d593.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AI\\cdot IL = PI\\cdot QI$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"143\" height=\"16\" /> by Power of a Point. Therefore, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/2/9/f29ec7efaf5d4d687d2e1dc2931b372f002bc355.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r\\rho = PI \\cdot QI = (PO + OI)(QO - OI) = (r + d)(r - d)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"449\" height=\"20\" />, and we have <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027bef297f1908a10814a041538cc77f50bec7f4.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2r\\rho = r^2 - d^2 \\iff d = \\sqrt {r(r - 2\\rho)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"286\" height=\"35\" />, and we are done.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_6&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO\" title=\"1962 IMO\">1962 IMO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems\">Problems</a></b>) • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c3222\">Resources</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">Problem 5</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">6</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1962_IMO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1962 IMO Problems/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td align=\"center\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=IMO_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"IMO Problems and Solutions\"> All IMO Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017164014\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.028 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.042 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 170/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 894/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 44/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4962/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    7.620      1 Template:IMO_box\n100.00%    7.620      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:7544:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017164014 and revision id 207709. Rendering was triggered because: api-parse\n -->\n</div>"}